  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-22T00:49:35.700Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've noticed a weird issue with physbones and how they sync over platforms. Imagine this, an avatar with a tail, ears, tong, etc. The PC model has everything extra, and dose not have a hard limit. So the Quest model needs to be limited to 8, in which case you now need to delete unneeded physbone scripts like the tong. Once this happens you get this weird desync. A Quest user pulls to ears, and as a PC player you see nothing, or sometimes in weird cases the PC users sees the Quest user pulling there tong. I've ran into this issue as my avatar has physbones in the hoodie strings, which I use to control the hood, it also has extra dynamics in the fluff, etc. I needed to remove the unneeded dynamics, which made it Quest compatible. But now when a Quest user pulls my hoodie strings, they grab my nose, and the hood never goes up.",
